  "id": "holography",
  "term": "holography",
  "definition": "In this source, holography refers to a proposed neurophysically grounded account of consciousness in which probabilistic cortical computation is used to explain how biophysical brain activity gives rise to phenomenal or perceptual experience. It is presented as a specific framework for naturalizing consciousness by treating conscious experience as continuous with processes studied in the natural sciences.",
